  "instructions": [
    "Preheat a grill or grill pan to medium-high heat.",
    "Cut the dates in half lengthwise and set aside.",
    "In a small bowl, mix together chili powder, fish sauce (if using), lime juice, garlic, ginger, salt, and black pepper.",
    "Add the tempeh to the bowl and toss to coat with the spice mixture.",
    "Thread the marinated tempeh and dates onto skewers.",
    "Brush the coconut oil onto the skewers and grill for 2-3 minutes per side, or until slightly charred.",
    "Transfer the skewers to a plate and garnish with chopped cilantro.",
    "Drizzle with palm sugar syrup (see note) if desired.",
    "Serve immediately and enjoy!",
    "Note: To make palm sugar syrup, combine 1 tablespoon palm sugar with 2 tablespoons water in a small saucepan and heat until dissolved."
  ],
